# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FreshNow demo environment — copy to `.env` and fill in.
# NEVER commit `.env`. The values below are placeholders, not real secrets.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database (Docker Postgres + pgvector) ───────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_USER=freshnow
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change_me_dev_only
POSTGRES_DB=freshnow
# App connects over localhost; the container port is published to 127.0.0.1 only.
# Host port is 5433 (not 5432) to avoid clashing with any existing local Postgres.
# App role = RLS-enforced (freshnow_app). Service role = owner/superuser (BYPASSRLS).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://freshnow_app:freshnow_app_pw@localhost:5433/freshnow
DATABASE_URL_SERVICE=postgresql://freshnow:change_me_dev_only@localhost:5433/freshnow
# Throwaway DB the test suite creates/migrates (never the demo DB).
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://freshnow_app:freshnow_app_pw@localhost:5433/freshnow_test
TEST_DATABASE_URL_SERVICE=postgresql://freshnow:change_me_dev_only@localhost:5433/freshnow_test

# ── Redis (Docker) — BullMQ queues + delayed SLA jobs ───────────────────
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# ── LLM: primary = Groq, fallback = OpenRouter, last resort = NVIDIA NIM ─
# Groq keys start with `gsk_`  →  https://console.groq.com
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your_key_here
GROQ_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# Verified available on Groq 2026-09-04: openai/gpt-oss-120b, openai/gpt-oss-20b, qwen/qwen3.8-27b
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# OpenRouter keys start with `sk-or-v1-`  ->  https://openrouter.ai/keys
# An INDEPENDENT company from Groq, so one outage cannot take out both. Paid models need
# credit on the account (5.5% fee when buying). Benchmarked 2026-09-12: gpt-4o-mini correct
# on every task; see docs/reports/model-benchmark.html before changing the model.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your_key_here
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
# Provider order, first to last. Anything configured but not listed is tried after these.
# LLM_PROVIDER_ORDER=groq,openrouter,nvidia
# NVIDIA NIM keys start with `nvapi-`  →  https://build.nvidia.com
NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-your_key_here
NVIDIA_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
NVIDIA_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning
# Hard daily LLM spend cap (USD). On breach the system degrades to rules-only. Counted from
# llm_call.cost_usd: the provider bill when it sends one (OpenRouter), else list price x tokens
# (packages/core/src/llm/cost.ts) — so a free-tier Groq call still counts at paid-tier price.
LLM_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=2

# ── Telegram (ONE bot serves both the CEO and employees) ────────────────
# Token from @BotFather, looks like 8123456789:AAH... — keep secret.
# Optional for the WORKER since TASK-044: with no token it starts without a Telegram sender,
# which is how an "App only" deployment (inbox + web push, no Telegram) runs.
BOT_TOKEN=
# Numeric Telegram user id of the CEO (from @userinfobot). Stored as bigint.
CEO_TELEGRAM_USER_ID=
# Local demo uses long polling (no public URL). Production: webhook + Caddy TLS.
TELEGRAM_MODE=polling
# Only used when TELEGRAM_MODE=webhook (verifies X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token).
TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Misc ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Store UTC in the DB, render Asia/Dubai. UAE working week is Mon–Fri.
TZ=Asia/Dubai
NODE_ENV=development

# Optional shared secret for the dashboard and its API.
#
# The API binds 0.0.0.0 so a phone on the same wifi can reach it. Without Supabase (below)
# there is NO login.
# Left unset (the demo default) anyone on that network can read every employee's data and
# use the natural-language query box. Set this and every /dashboard/* request must carry it
# as ?k=<token> or an X-Dashboard-Key header.
# DASHBOARD_TOKEN=change-me-to-something-long

# ── Supabase: dashboard sign-in and the production database ──────────────────
# With SUPABASE_URL set, every /dashboard/* and /employees/* request must carry a Supabase
# Auth JWT, and the viewer is the employee linked to that account (?viewer= is ignored).
# Leave it unset for demo mode. Local stack: npx supabase start, then npx supabase status.
# SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# Public by design (it ships to every browser); the security is in verifying the JWT.
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_...
# Only for a project still on the legacy shared HS256 secret. Asymmetric keys need none.
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=
# Read ONLY by pnpm link:user to create dashboard accounts. It bypasses RLS through the
# Data API, so the API, bot and worker never read it. Keep it out of any shared file.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...
#
# Database on Supabase: the app role stays RLS-enforced; the service role is postgres
# (BYPASSRLS, not superuser). The local stack publishes Postgres on port 54322.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://freshnow_app:<app-password>@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
# DATABASE_URL_SERVICE=postgresql://postgres:<password>@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# ── Langfuse: LLM tracing (optional, off unless BOTH keys are set) ───────────
# Turns every model call into a trace you can read as a story: which provider answered,
# how long it took, what it cost, and where a retry fell through to a fallback. The
# `llm_call` table remains the record of cost (the budget cap reads it and must not depend
# on a third party); Langfuse is the timeline on top of it.
#
# Get the keys from the Langfuse UI: Settings -> API Keys -> Create new API key.
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-...
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-...
#
# Defaults to a self-hosted instance on this machine, where nothing leaves the box.
# Point it at https://cloud.langfuse.com (EU) or https://us.cloud.langfuse.com for cloud.
# LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# ⚠️  PROMPTS CONTAIN EMPLOYEES' OWN WORDS. Leave this unset and only metadata is sent —
# model, provider, tokens, cost, latency, success — which answers every question about cost
# and reliability. Set it to 1 and the prompt and completion TEXT go too. With a hosted
# Langfuse that means employee free text leaves the company, which needs the same lawful
# basis, notice and consent as any other processing (UAE PDPL). Off by default on purpose.
# LANGFUSE_CAPTURE_CONTENT=1
#
# Optional: tags every trace with a build, so a change in behaviour can be tied to a deploy.
# LANGFUSE_RELEASE=2026-09-14

# ── Model-call concurrency (PER PROCESS) ─────────────────────────────────────
# The API and the bot each cap their own concurrent model calls at this number; the real
# ceiling against the provider is the SUM of the two. Default 2 each (4 total). Groq's
# on-demand tier is 8 000 tokens/min, and a document plan is ~2 350 tokens — size this to
# the tier you are on, not to how fast you would like it to be.
# LLM_CONCURRENCY=2

# ── Telegram webhook mode (production) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Long polling is the default and needs nothing. Webhook mode needs ALL THREE below; the
# bot refuses to start without them rather than listening unverified. Caddy proxies
# PUBLIC_URL + TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_PATH to 127.0.0.1:TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_PORT.
# TELEGRAM_MODE=webhook
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<at least 16 random characters — Telegram sends it back on every delivery>
# PUBLIC_URL=https://ops.example.ae
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_PATH=/telegram/webhook
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_PORT=3002

# ── PDPL retention ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Days after which an employee's FREE TEXT (what they typed) is redacted. Counts, statuses,
# blockers and the audit trail are never touched. Unset = nothing is aged out, and the
# worker says so every hour. This number is the data controller's decision — see
# docs/WHAT-WE-NEED-FROM-FRESHNOW.md §3. Values under 30 are refused.
# RETENTION_DAYS=365

# ── Security: virus scanning and backups (TASK-051, COMMANDS.md §7d–7e) ──────────
# ClamAV scans every attached file before anything opens it. Start it with
#   docker compose --profile security up -d clamav      (first start downloads signatures: minutes)
# Once CLAMAV_HOST is set, a file that cannot be scanned is REFUSED (fail closed). Unset = not
# scanned (the demo default). Production refuses to start without it (policy rule R6).
# CLAMAV_HOST=127.0.0.1
# CLAMAV_PORT=3310
# CLAMAV_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
#
# `pnpm backup`: where dumps go, how many to keep, and the age PUBLIC key they are encrypted to
# (age-keygen -o freshnow-backup.key, on a machine that is NOT the server; keep that file offline).
# BACKUP_DIR=backups
# BACKUP_KEEP=14
# BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT=age1...
# Only where you run backup:verify / backup:restore-test on an encrypted file — the PRIVATE key:
# BACKUP_AGE_IDENTITY=C:\path\to\freshnow-backup.key
# pg_dump runs inside this container when it is running (auto-detected); "none" = local pg_dump.
# BACKUP_PG_CONTAINER=supabase_db_freshnow

# ── Demo badge ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# true (default) shows the DEMO badge in the dashboard and on the entry screens, meaning the
# data is synthetic. Set to false on the production box once real company data is in.
# IS_DEMO=false

# ── Web push (PWA notifications) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# A second channel that costs nothing and belongs to nobody: VAPID is a key pair you
# generate yourself, and the push relays (Google FCM, Apple APNs, Mozilla) accept it with
# no account and no API key. Generate once with `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`;
# rotating them unsubscribes every device.
#
# Push and service workers only run in a SECURE CONTEXT — https://, or http://localhost.
# On a LAN address like http://10.0.0.5:3001 nothing here activates, by browser design.
# Without these three, "App only" is refused in the dashboard: switching Telegram off with no
# push to replace it would leave people reachable only while the dashboard is open.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=<the public key>
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=<the private key>
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:ops@yourdomain.ae

# ── Email ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any SMTP provider works. Brevo's free tier (300/day) covers this system's volume; Resend
# and SMTP2GO are drop-in. Needs a domain with SPF/DKIM/DMARC — docs/EMAIL-SETUP-GUIDE.md.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=<the provider's user>
# SMTP_PASS=<the provider's key>
# EMAIL_FROM="FreshNow Ops <ops@yourdomain.ae>"
#
# Inbound: Cloudflare Email Routing (free) posts a forwarded email here, which becomes a
# PROPOSAL the CEO confirms — never a silent write. The secret is checked in constant time
# and SPF/DKIM/DMARC must pass, because inbound mail is otherwise a spoofable write path.
# INBOUND_EMAIL_SECRET=<at least 16 random characters>

# ── Company chat (Mattermost / Slack-compatible incoming webhook) ────────────
# Optional. docs/MATTERMOST-SETUP-GUIDE.md covers standing the server up; nothing starts
# unless you start it.
# CHAT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://chat.yourdomain.ae/hooks/<id>
